Feature: Scene Detection Pipeline — Real AI Engine Integration
  As a platform operator
  I want scene detection to use real AI engines (YOLO) instead of mock random data
  So that detected surfaces reflect actual video content and are useful for ad placement

  Background:
    Given the BIT platform has a content ingestion pipeline
    And AI engine configuration is managed via Platform Settings

  Scenario: Scene detection uses real YOLO engine by default
    Given the platform setting "engine_detection" is set to "yolo"
    And the Python YOLO detection service is running on port 8001
    When I run scene detection on an uploaded video
    Then the Hangfire background job is enqueued
    And the YOLO service is called for each detected scene
    And real surface detections are persisted to the database
    And NO random mock surfaces are generated

  Scenario: Scene detection fails clearly when YOLO is unreachable
    Given the platform setting "engine_detection" is set to "yolo"
    And the Python YOLO detection service is NOT running
    When I run scene detection on an uploaded video
    Then the Hangfire job fails with a clear error message
    And the content status is set to "Failed"
    And the error message indicates the YOLO service is unreachable
    And NO random mock surfaces are generated as fallback

  Scenario: Basic engine throws instead of generating mock data
    Given the platform setting "engine_detection" is set to "basic"
    When the detection engine is invoked
    Then an InvalidOperationException is thrown
    And the error message instructs the operator to configure a real engine

  Scenario: Single-scene video produces exactly one scene
    Given a video with no scene changes (continuous footage)
    When I run scene detection
    Then exactly 1 scene is created covering the entire video duration
    And no artificial 30-second scene chunks are generated

  Scenario: Re-detect scenes enqueues the Hangfire job
    Given a content item that has completed scene detection
    When I click "Re-detect Scenes"
    Then the content transitions to SceneDetecting stage
    And a Hangfire background job is enqueued
    And the job runs the full detection pipeline
    And old scenes and surfaces are deleted before new ones are created

  Scenario: Scene detection generates surface thumbnails
    Given scene detection completes successfully with detected surfaces
    When the detection pipeline finishes
    Then each surface has a thumbnail image saved to Uploads/thumbnails/
    And the PlacementImageUrl field is set to the thumbnail path
    And failed thumbnail generation does not block the pipeline

  Scenario: Re-detect does not fail when already in SceneDetecting
    Given a content item whose status is "SceneDetecting"
    When I click "Re-detect Scenes"
    Then the pipeline transition is skipped (no self-transition error)
    And the Hangfire job is still enqueued
    And the detection pipeline runs normally

  Scenario: Re-detect enqueues exactly one Hangfire job
    Given a content item eligible for re-detection
    When I click "Re-detect Scenes"
    Then exactly ONE Hangfire background job is enqueued
    And the frontend does NOT also call /api/video/ai-split-analyze
    And the frontend polls /api/content/{id}/detection-status for completion
    And on completion, scenes are refreshed and the first scene is auto-selected
